{
  "dom_id": "step-q94601",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Find the median of the random variable $X$ if the cumulative distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0, \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{144}, & 0\\le x\\le 12, \\\\ 1, & x>12.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "The median of a random variable $X$ is the number $m$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le m)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nP(X\\le m)=F(m)=\\frac{{m}^{2}}{144},\\,0\\le m\\le 12.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the median is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{m}^{2}}{144}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⇒\\,m=6\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nNote that we took the positive root because $0\\le m\\le 12.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
